> - `javascript/api.py` defines `javascript_tool_manifest` and `javascript_control_description` twice; the latter definitions silently override the registry-safe versions.
> - `validate.py` is regex-based and presently cannot enforce loop/operation bounds or safely distinguish identifiers/comments/strings. It should remain a conservative prefilter until AST validation is available.
> - JS-exposed tools are manifest-derived, but execution does not yet resolve pinned manifest entries into `ToolInvocation → ToolResult`.
> - `llm_text` needs a registered tool adapter that either honors an explicit model ID or invokes Planner’s normal model-selection path.
> - `Planner` currently selects a normal responder first; integration needs a planning-model turn using `javascript_prompt(registry)`, then `extract_plan`, response-record persistence, synchronous plan execution, and trace/artifact persistence.
> - `ResponseRecord` needs either explicit plan-run/trace/artifact fields or a durable linked execution-record type for complete provenance and recursive feedback attribution.
> 
> Please provide the existing `worker.js` (if any), the desired JS engine choice (Deno or QuickJS), and whether you want a minimal end-to-end v1 first or the full recursive-budgeted execution model.
